<title>USA: Panel to review U.S. electric reliability councils.</title>
<headline>Panel to review U.S. electric reliability councils.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Deputy Energy Secretary Charles Curtis Thursday urged a new panel to study whether voluntary efforts among utilities to maintain a reliable power grid would be good enough to ensure a stable electric system when power markets are fully open to competition.</p>
<p>Curtis spoke at the first meeting of a panel appointed by the Energy Department to review electricity reliability in light of restructuring in the industry and two major power outages in the western states last summer.</p>
</text>
